From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 02:10:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] propsys: Convert more types to strings.

PropVariantToStringAlloc, and through it PropVariantToString and
PropVariantToBSTR, knew strings, integers and CLSIDs; VariantToString
only a BSTR and a 32-bit integer.  The tests fix how Windows writes the
rest: a boolean as its number, floats as written, a FILETIME and a DATE
as yyyy/mm/dd:hh:mm:ss.mmm, the elements of a vector between "; ", and an
empty VARIANT as an empty string.  Both now format one value at a time
the same way.  A SAFEARRAY, which Excel and PowerPoint hand
VariantToString at startup, is still refused, for want of knowing how
Windows writes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

